                        "entry_id": "c289e9f9-e58d-337c-8a00-d83417ae81dc",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Any myriapod which rolls up for protection; a galleyworm."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "rare"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "18691855-9387-4e67-945e-f0da86ea6c25",
                                "sense_id": "ff135bf9-da9e-332b-9d2f-43e27cde7c9d",
                                "text": "Another one (Armadillo rugulosus) is endowed with the power of rolling itself up in a ball like the \"pill-worm\" of the Old Country"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2d10e837-3261-45bc-81eb-4b4e0ca4282b",
                                "sense_id": "ff135bf9-da9e-332b-9d2f-43e27cde7c9d",
                                "text": "Objects of the Scheme:—(1) To produce intra hissutum and hissutum barbadense hybrids (F₁₁) possessing resistance to blackarm, red leaf blight and pillworm besides having economic and agronomic values and suitable for growing as such or by budding on perennial of stocks."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "25ca2f4f-2f6f-47e2-bce0-2f5c02e98378",
                                "sense_id": "ff135bf9-da9e-332b-9d2f-43e27cde7c9d",
                                "text": "The PILLWORM is restless, aggressive, and nearly as destructive as, though more sophisticated than, the APHID."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "3e12003b-5e23-401d-a193-c8328d60d66a",
                                "sense_id": "ff135bf9-da9e-332b-9d2f-43e27cde7c9d",
                                "text": "The high beach inhabitants include different kinds of periwinkles, a burrowing worm called the pill worm, and the beach hoppers that often parade along the beach in great numbers in early morning or twilight."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "4cb042f4-fe90-4b20-b34a-d40dcc600e4b",
                                "sense_id": "ff135bf9-da9e-332b-9d2f-43e27cde7c9d",
                                "text": "an event which happened years earlier had eaten away at the parish in his charge as a pillworm eats at a plant."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
